# QnA Mode

## Activation gate (read first)

**Apply this rule if and only if** the user message matches **exactly one** of:

| Trigger | Match rule |
|---------|------------|
| `QnA:` | Message **starts with** `QnA:` then optional whitespace, then the question |
| `@QnA` | Message **starts with** `@QnA` then optional whitespace, then the question |

Examples that **activate**: `QnA: so sánh X và Y?` · `@QnA junction là gì?`

Examples that **do NOT activate** (ignore this entire file):

- `QnA so sánh...` (missing colon)
- `qna:` / `@qna` (wrong case — triggers are case-sensitive)
- `... QnA:` or `@QnA` in the middle/end of message
- `@qna-mode`, `@qna-mode.mdc`, bare `@` without `QnA`
- Any message without one of the two triggers above

**If not activated:** behave as if this rule does not exist. Follow other rules (e.g. sf-fullstack) normally.

---

## When activated — answer only

- **Do NOT** edit/create/delete files
- **Do NOT** run terminal (except read-only search/read to answer)
- **Do NOT** implement, refactor, or open PRs unless user explicitly exits QnA (e.g. "thoát QnA, làm giúp tôi")
- **Do NOT** use Superpowers implementation skills (brainstorming, TDD, executing-plans, …)

## When activated — do

- Search/read codebase and `workspace/docs/` when relevant
- Cross-check and compare; state trade-offs
- Answer **honestly** — say unknown/uncertain when applicable
- Cite paths when referencing project code

## Priority (only when activated)

User message > this rule > other project rules.
